---
title: "7 · Send for e-signature"
description: Send a ready contract for signing online, follow the client's signing and receive the signed copy.
sidebar:
  order: 8
  label: "7 · Send for e-signature"
---

**Who:** the person in charge. **Where:** step 4 **Signing**.

The firm always signs with the saved signature of its signatory (see [1 · Contract settings](/en/crm/templates/)) and is never sent the contract. Only the client is invited to sign.

- **Engagement letter** and **Quotation**: the firm's saved signature is applied before the contract is sent, so the client receives a copy that already carries it.
- **VIP contract**: once the client has signed, Operon countersigns automatically with the saved signature, and with the company seal when one is registered for the issuing entity.

{% steps %}

1. When the contract is **Ready to send**, check the signers on the **Send for signature** card. The **Service provider** row shows the firm's signatory with **Saved signature**. On the **Client** row, choose **Online** or **Paper**.
2. If someone should be kept informed, select **+ Add CC** and enter the name and email. CC recipients get an email when signing starts, each time someone signs, and a download link when everyone has signed. The client does not see who is copied.
3. To change the wording of the invitation, reminder and completion emails for this contract only, select **Email content**.
4. Select **Send**. The signature boxes are placed from the marks in the template; nothing has to be dragged. For an edited draft that lost a mark, place the boxes first with **Check signature boxes**.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="crm/signing-ready" caption="Approved and ready to send." /%}

If the contract cannot be sent, the reason is shown next to **Send**, for example when the Director in charge has no active saved signature. A tenant admin adds it under **Contract signatories** in CRM settings.

## Follow the signing

The card shows each signer's status (**Not opened**, **Viewed**, **Signed** …) and the date on which the signing link expires. For the client you can select **Send reminder**, **Change email** or **Switch to paper**. When a link has expired, select **Extend and resend**. **Open in E-sign** in the contract header opens the signing request itself in a new tab.

{% screenshot id="crm/signing-sent" caption="Sent: each signer's status and link expiry." /%}

## When everyone has signed

The contract becomes **Signed**, and the signed PDF is filed in the opportunity's files automatically. If filing fails, it is tried again every 15 minutes; until then the signed copy can be downloaded on the card.

If the client declines to sign, the reason is shown, the contract goes back to the Signing step, and you can select **Send again**.

{% aside type="caution" title="If the automatic countersignature fails" %}
For a VIP contract, the card shows **Our signature could not be applied** with the reason. Select **Switch to paper signing**, then upload the signed copy to finish the contract.
{% /aside %}
